  "Each environment is deterministic: two runs give bit-identical calibrated.rou.xml.",
  "Python 3.9.6 -> 3.12.15 has no effect: E1 is bit-identical to E0.",
  "The candidate route pool and trip generation are bit-identical across all environments; candidates.meta.json differs only in route_cost_s at the 12th significant digit (float summation order).",
  "scipy 1.13.1 -> 1.18.1 alone reproduces the whole difference: E3 is bit-identical to E2.",
  "Mechanism: the integer projection MILP in traffic_sim/demand/pfe.py has non-unique optima. HiGHS 1.2.0 and 1.12.0 return different, equally optimal solutions for identical problems, and later problems inherit the difference.",
  "Same sensor fit is not equivalence: both hit 672/672 integer sensor targets exactly, yet through 380->288, external 1798->1640, service 4624->4879 vehicles."
 ],
 "consequence": "Results are reproducible only with the exact solver version, which requirements.lock now pins (scipy==1.18.1). The choice among tied optima is arbitrary with respect to the model; a deterministic, solver-independent tie-break would be a model change and is out of scope for this migration."
